{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BTyn7bsKbC7ucB2pniQCPk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Gap hunt: C04 — Detect drift per agent\n2\t\n3\tA reviewer couldn't decide whether this item is met. **Your job is to find out whether any\n4\tcheck below is false in this codebase.** The reviewer's partial answers and the code they\n5\tlooked at are shown. Read the code, and open the repo files the checks point to.\n6\t\n7\tFor each check, decide:\n8\t- **fails**: you found the line that makes it false (a missing control, a bypass, a\n9\t  value never used, an exception that continues, a filter that lets something through).\n10\t  Quote that line;\n11\t- **holds**: you found the code that makes it true in every case;\n12\t- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n13\t\n14\t**The requirement for C04:** Compare running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, and self-hosted model weights against their approved baseline. Simulate a prompt edit, an added tool, and a looser egress rule. Check that each one raises an alert and gets the documented response — block, quarantine, or rollback — within a set time.\n15\t\n16\tIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n17\t`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n18\t\n19\t\n20\t## C04.1\n21\t\n22\t**Check:** A drift check compares running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, and self-hosted model weights against the approved baseline, with each of these covered.\n23\t\n24\t**How to verify:** 1) Find the drift check job or tool. 2) List what it compares: images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, self-hosted weights. 3) Check each is compared with the approved baseline, not with the live state itself. 4) Answer no if any category is missing or excluded. Answer unknown if drift detection runs in an outside platform.\n25\t\n26\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n27\t\n28\t**Reviewer's note:** CI manifest-check compares prompt digests only; no running-state drift check in repo, may be in the platform\n29\t\n30\t(no evidence cited)\n31\t\n32\t## C04.2\n33\t\n34\t**Check:** The drift check runs per agent deployment, on a schedule or on change events.\n35\t\n36\t**How to verify:** 1) Find what triggers the drift check: cron or CI schedule, admission webhook, or change events. 2) Check it runs for each agent deployment, not once for the fleet or only by hand. 3) Answer no if it is manual-only or covers only some deployments. Answer unknown if scheduling is set outside this repo.\n37\t\n38\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n39\t\n40\t**Reviewer's note:** No scheduled drift job found in repo; may be set outside\n41\t\n42\t(no evidence cited)\n43\t\n44\t## C04.3\n45\t\n46\t**Check:** Detected drift triggers an alert and a set response (block, quarantine, or rollback) defined in config, with a time limit.\n47\t\n48\t**How to verify:** 1) Open the drift check's result handling. 2) Check drift raises an alert and triggers a response set in config: block, quarantine, or rollback. 3) Check a time limit is set. 4) Answer no if drift only logs, the response or time limit is missing, or a check error is treated as no drift.\n49\t\n50\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n51\t\n52\t**Reviewer's note:** No drift alert or response config found in repo\n53\t\n54\t(no evidence cited)\n55\t\n56\t## Your answer\n57\t\n58\tWrite this JSON to C04.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"C04\"):\n59\t```json\n60\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n61\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"C04.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n62\t \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n63\t```\n64\tVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c55835ff-11a5-465a-8aba-ef91484ef06b","uuid":"188c5e83-8c6d-440d-8959-4f5a8168e060","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:51:02.530Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-uhqaxytn/sheet.md","content":"# Gap hunt: C04 — Detect drift per agent\n\nA reviewer couldn't decide whether this item is met. **Your job is to find out whether any\ncheck below is false in this codebase.** The reviewer's partial answers and the code they\nlooked at are shown. Read the code, and open the repo files the checks point to.\n\nFor each check, decide:\n- **fails**: you found the line that makes it false (a missing control, a bypass, a\n  value never used, an exception that continues, a filter that lets something through).\n  Quote that line;\n- **holds**: you found the code that makes it true in every case;\n- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n\n**The requirement for C04:** Compare running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, and self-hosted model weights against their approved baseline. Simulate a prompt edit, an added tool, and a looser egress rule. Check that each one raises an alert and gets the documented response — block, quarantine, or rollback — within a set time.\n\nIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n\n\n## C04.1\n\n**Check:** A drift check compares running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, and self-hosted mod